Z||000000||spideyfoot||06-16-2001||09:16 PM||||Well my little car left me stranded today. Overheated way quick. Got to ride the rollback home. Turns out belt came off its an 88 duke. Anyone have any special tricks or knowledge to share about installing new one. I don't even see how I am going to reach down there. The Chilton tells nothing on this. I  going to wait and do this the right way so I don't screw it up any help would be appreciated. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-16-2001||09:24 PM||||read the belt article in my cave. Tells you everything you need to know about serpents. have someone get under the car to put/hold the belt on the low pulleys. Much easier, especially the first time you try it.<P>buy a serpent wrench. You can get them at many autoparts stores. $15-30us. Works much better than plain socket wrench.||||reg||1
